item.text:
OK so the Input component wraps its children in a FieldWrapper which adds a Label and Error. For a standalone search input, this is overkill. 

I think the pragmatic approach is to create a reusable `SearchInput` component that reuses the same input CSS classes (from the form Input) but without the form context. I'll place it in the toolbar component itself.

